From ca31f73e046c387a5232637fb1d6db7db78ae40c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:13:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV archive seam: pre-RoPE capture
 hook and cache restore API

Add an optional, disabled-by-default backend seam for causal self-attention
KV caches (runtime/layers/kvcache/causal_kv_backend.py):

- CausalWanSelfAttention hands the normalized pre-RoPE key and the value of
  each layer to an active capture scope before _apply_rotary_emb. No scope is
  active unless a backend opened one for a clean context forward, so the
  dense path is unchanged (one None check, no copies).
- Attention modules get a layer index from their transformer.
- CausalWanTransformer3DModel.causal_rotary_cos_sin is the single source of
  the (cos, sin) tables used by forward, so restored keys can be re-rotated
  with the engine's own RoPE at their original positions; causal_rotate_key
  exposes the key rotation itself.
- CausalSelfAttentionKVCache.replay_layout replays the cache's own cursor,
  eviction and pinned-sink logic on a CPU position shadow to compute the slot
  layout after a sequence of chunk appends and the slots the next chunk
  attends to; install_restored_history zeroes the live slots of a reset cache,
  lets the backend write restored post-RoPE K / V into the attended slots and
  sets the cursors and pinned shot sink.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
